 "text": "Can we talk about how people are casually paying seven hundred and fifty dollars a month for a car? Like, that's actually crazy to me. And the worst part? That's just the car payment. You still gotta pay insurance, gas, maintenance, all that. Let's say you're paying two hundred dollars for insurance and another two hundred dollars for gas. Bro, that's one thousand one hundred and fifty dollars a month just to drive your car. That's almost fourteen thousand dollars a year, and we haven't even talked about tires or repairs yet. Now, imagine what you could do with even half of that money. You could be saving, investing, traveling, actually enjoying your life. And look, I'm not saying you shouldn't have a nice car. If you can comfortably afford it, go for it. But me personally, I'd rather get a good, reliable used car and keep that extra money in my pocket. Because what's the point of driving a nice car if you're stressed about money every single month? But I'm curious, what's the most you'd be willing to pay for a car payment?",
